      "publication_year": 2019,
      "publication_date": "2019-10-30",
      "abstract": "Focusing on the conceptual terms of the idealist-realist debate, the paper shows that the inability of the realists to recognize Marx\u2019s idealist heritage is out of the realists\u2019 limited understanding of the category of idealism in their reading. To prove the paper\u2019s case, the first section starts with elucidation of Marx\u2019s concept of epistemological idealism as read by his interpreters. It shows the actual meaning of epistemological idealism as used by Kolakowski, Lukacs, and other idealist readers of Marx. The second section shows how the realists conflate the two idealisms, how the realist reading is erroneously grounded on failure to clarify the difference between the concept of ontological and epistemological idealism. The third section highlights the differences between epistemological and ontological idealism. It explains that Ontological idealism claims that idea is the fundamental reality, while epistemological idealism suggests that knowledge is dependent upon the subject.",
